1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:13,620
Good morning.

2
00:00:18,040 --> 00:00:20,160
Whoa, the wind is strong today.

3
00:00:20,420 --> 00:00:22,600
No joke, not to mention it's freezing out here.

4
00:00:22,740 --> 00:00:24,360
It feels like fall. Did you hear?

5
00:00:24,560 --> 00:00:25,500
Huh? Hear what?

6
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:36,120
I guess it's the season for warm drinks now.

7
00:00:38,980 --> 00:00:41,400
Looks like autumn has finally arrived.

8
00:00:42,360 --> 00:00:46,080
As seasons must change, I'm feeling left behind again.

9
00:00:48,780 --> 00:00:50,840
There she is! Hanabi!

10
00:00:54,660 --> 00:00:58,580
I'm sorry, but you were absent when we were picking roles for the school festival.

11
00:00:58,580 --> 00:01:01,720
Hey, I hope you don't mind just being a stagehand, Hanabi.

12
00:01:02,560 --> 00:01:05,360
Uh, stage? What do I need to do?

13
00:01:05,900 --> 00:01:09,960
Oh, don't worry. Just leave the heavy lifting to the band club and you'll be fine.

14
00:01:10,320 --> 00:01:10,840
Mm-hmm.

15
00:01:11,440 --> 00:01:15,580
You only have to do the easy work, like watching over the schedule and stuff. Please?

16
00:01:18,380 --> 00:01:21,140
Hanabi, that's why you should go meet with them.

17
00:01:25,560 --> 00:01:27,240
Alright, I'll do it.

18
00:01:27,240 --> 00:01:31,440
That's awesome! Now everyone has a job!

19
00:01:31,860 --> 00:01:32,920
Thank you, Hanabi!

20
00:01:42,920 --> 00:01:44,820
Wow, that's already cold.

21
00:01:44,820 --> 00:01:46,680
Mookie.

22
00:01:57,820 --> 00:02:02,440
Mookie...

23
00:02:03,440 --> 00:02:04,440
Mookie...

24
00:03:33,947 --> 00:03:37,947
The wedding is coming up. They're having it over spring break.

25
00:03:38,947 --> 00:03:42,947
Brother came by. He thought it would be best if I heard it from him.

26
00:03:43,947 --> 00:03:44,947
Huh?

27
00:03:45,947 --> 00:03:46,947
Hana?

28
00:03:50,947 --> 00:03:51,947
Congratulations.

29
00:03:52,947 --> 00:03:55,947
We talked a bit. On our way home.

30
00:03:56,947 --> 00:03:57,947
Poor Mugi.

31
00:03:57,947 --> 00:04:00,947
I guess it didn't work out. Serves him right, though.

32
00:04:02,947 --> 00:04:04,947
Are you surprised it's so sudden?

33
00:04:04,947 --> 00:04:06,947
No, I'm not surprised at all.

34
00:04:06,947 --> 00:04:08,947
Really? Why not?

35
00:04:08,947 --> 00:04:12,947
Because it was really obvious to me. I knew you were in love with her.

36
00:04:16,947 --> 00:04:19,947
So what's this? You stopped wearing glasses.

37
00:04:19,947 --> 00:04:23,947
Huh? Yeah. I broke my glasses. So I just...

38
00:04:24,947 --> 00:04:26,947
She asked you to wear contacts, didn't she?

39
00:04:26,947 --> 00:04:28,947
What? How did you know?

40
00:04:28,947 --> 00:04:33,947
It's so obvious. But for the record, I preferred you in glasses.

41
00:04:33,947 --> 00:04:34,947
Ugh.

42
00:04:35,947 --> 00:04:36,947
Because...

43
00:04:37,947 --> 00:04:39,947
The way he looks right now...

44
00:04:40,947 --> 00:04:42,947
Reminds me of the days when he was just mine.

45
00:04:43,947 --> 00:04:44,947
And...

46
00:04:44,947 --> 00:04:46,947
It still kind of hurts.

47
00:04:48,947 --> 00:04:50,947
Hana, will you come to the wedding?

48
00:04:50,947 --> 00:04:51,947
Hana?

49
00:05:08,947 --> 00:05:09,947
Yeah.

50
00:05:10,947 --> 00:05:11,947
I'll be there.

51
00:05:12,947 --> 00:05:13,947
Of course I will.

52
00:05:13,947 --> 00:05:14,947
I'll be there.

53
00:05:14,947 --> 00:05:15,947
I'll be there.

54
00:05:18,947 --> 00:05:19,947
Thank you.

55
00:05:28,947 --> 00:05:29,947
Right this way, please.

56
00:05:32,947 --> 00:05:33,947
Would you like some cheese?

57
00:05:34,947 --> 00:05:37,947
Okay. So this will be our final schedule for the rest of the festival day.

58
00:05:37,947 --> 00:05:40,947
I'm sure you're all tired by now from all the prepping you've been doing.

59
00:05:41,947 --> 00:05:42,947
But let's do it!

60
00:05:43,947 --> 00:05:45,947
Dude, look at her. Her eyes are glazed over.

61
00:05:46,947 --> 00:05:49,947
Wait, wasn't she the one who was all about building this stage in the first place?

62
00:05:50,947 --> 00:05:51,947
You two over there! Students A and B!

63
00:05:52,947 --> 00:05:54,947
If you're late at any point today, I'm throwing you in the bonfire!

64
00:05:55,947 --> 00:05:57,947
Wow. I'm just glad things came together in the end.

65
00:05:58,947 --> 00:05:59,947
Hey!

66
00:06:00,947 --> 00:06:02,947
Oh, my date made it here.

67
00:06:02,947 --> 00:06:03,947
So you're off with your boyfriend?

68
00:06:04,947 --> 00:06:05,947
Try not to be late!

69
00:06:06,947 --> 00:06:07,947
What's up? Do you not have time?

70
00:06:08,947 --> 00:06:09,947
Yeah, I have plenty of time.

71
00:06:10,947 --> 00:06:11,947
Although, I am a bit tired.

72
00:06:12,947 --> 00:06:13,947
Did you need to go rest somewhere?

73
00:06:14,947 --> 00:06:15,947
No.

74
00:06:16,947 --> 00:06:18,947
Who do I really want to be with?

75
00:06:19,947 --> 00:06:23,947
I locked away the few names that popped into my head, quietly shutting them down.

76
00:06:24,947 --> 00:06:25,947
Where do you want to start?

77
00:06:26,947 --> 00:06:27,947
Hey, let's eat something first!

78
00:06:27,947 --> 00:06:28,947
Totally!

79
00:06:29,947 --> 00:06:31,947
Looks like I've got time before they need me back at the stage.

80
00:06:34,947 --> 00:06:36,947
Please come check us out!

81
00:06:37,947 --> 00:06:38,947
We're doing a fashion show!

82
00:06:39,947 --> 00:06:40,947
Why not come in and see?

83
00:06:41,947 --> 00:06:42,947
We have lots of great outfits to show!

84
00:06:43,947 --> 00:06:44,947
Hurry up or we'll miss it!

85
00:06:57,947 --> 00:06:58,947
Bye!

86
00:07:11,947 --> 00:07:12,947
Bye!

87
00:07:12,947 --> 00:07:31,327
That I've loved my precious Mookie much longer and more honestly than you could ever dream of.

88
00:07:36,187 --> 00:07:38,407
I feel refreshed and alive now.

89
00:07:38,407 --> 00:07:44,667
You'll understand once you bother doing something for your own well-being.

90
00:07:51,127 --> 00:07:52,887
Thank you for attending the show!

91
00:07:53,527 --> 00:07:55,867
Your dress was incredible, Miss Noriko.

92
00:07:56,107 --> 00:07:56,587
Really?

93
00:07:56,987 --> 00:07:58,647
The embroidery is so intricate.

94
00:07:58,907 --> 00:08:00,007
Did you do it all yourself?

95
00:08:00,467 --> 00:08:01,987
Yeah, amazing!

96
00:08:02,707 --> 00:08:04,647
Do you always make all of your films together?

97
00:08:04,927 --> 00:08:05,487
I do.

98
00:08:05,807 --> 00:08:07,247
Really? I thought so.

99
00:08:07,247 --> 00:08:08,767
I've been meaning to ask you a lot.

100
00:08:10,707 --> 00:08:13,127
Hey, will you teach me how to make clothes, Noriko?

101
00:08:13,547 --> 00:08:14,407
It's Moka!

102
00:08:14,907 --> 00:08:16,607
It's Moka!

103
00:08:18,887 --> 00:08:20,127
What do I want?

104
00:08:21,607 --> 00:08:22,907
I just don't know.

105
00:08:26,187 --> 00:08:27,727
You're late, Yasuraoka!

106
00:08:27,987 --> 00:08:29,447
Hurry up and help someone, will ya?

107
00:08:30,007 --> 00:08:31,347
Where is this box going?

108
00:08:31,487 --> 00:08:32,407
No, I'm gonna make it!

109
00:08:32,467 --> 00:08:33,747
Left, right, quick, quick, quick!

110
00:08:33,927 --> 00:08:34,767
Hurry up!

111
00:08:34,907 --> 00:08:35,467
Yes, ma'am!

112
00:08:35,467 --> 00:08:37,927
Hanabi, could you bring me the cord?

113
00:08:38,127 --> 00:08:38,747
Uh, yes!

114
00:08:39,687 --> 00:08:41,947
Sorry, Hanabi, can you help me with the flyers?

115
00:08:42,127 --> 00:08:43,207
Uh, sure, okay!

116
00:08:43,947 --> 00:08:46,667
Yasuraoka, take that equipment round to the back!

117
00:08:46,727 --> 00:08:47,527
Which one?

118
00:08:48,027 --> 00:08:48,767
That one!

119
00:08:48,867 --> 00:08:50,187
Now hurry up!

120
00:08:50,287 --> 00:08:50,707
Okay!

121
00:08:53,927 --> 00:08:55,367
Sorry, excuse me.

122
00:08:55,367 --> 00:08:57,247
Nobody's here.

123
00:08:57,247 --> 00:09:01,927
I'm so tired.

124
00:09:01,927 --> 00:09:05,907
I'm so tired.

125
00:09:11,327 --> 00:09:13,087
It feels nice to be alone.

126
00:09:13,907 --> 00:09:16,507
You can see things clearer when you're by yourself.

127
00:09:17,287 --> 00:09:17,887
That's right.

128
00:09:17,887 --> 00:09:20,227
I was alone to begin with.

129
00:09:20,807 --> 00:09:22,507
How could I have forgotten that?

130
00:09:23,767 --> 00:09:25,127
You scared of being alone?

131
00:09:25,427 --> 00:09:25,747
Mm-hmm.

132
00:09:27,987 --> 00:09:28,547
No.

133
00:09:29,347 --> 00:09:30,247
Not anymore.

134
00:09:31,247 --> 00:09:32,627
I was always alone.

135
00:09:33,587 --> 00:09:34,727
Everyone's alone, really.

136
00:09:37,547 --> 00:09:39,807
Then I guess this is meaningless, too.

137
00:09:39,807 --> 00:09:41,307
Yeah, it is.

138
00:09:41,307 --> 00:09:41,327
Yeah, it is.

139
00:09:42,087 --> 00:09:42,787
In the end.

140
00:09:45,147 --> 00:09:45,627
Mm-hmm.

141
00:09:49,587 --> 00:09:50,887
Why did we do it?

142
00:09:51,587 --> 00:09:53,067
Why did we make that promise?

143
00:09:53,647 --> 00:09:55,087
If it's all just meaningless?

144
00:10:00,647 --> 00:10:01,287
Why?

145
00:10:01,287 --> 00:10:07,687
I fell asleep.

146
00:10:11,067 --> 00:10:12,347
It hurt my shoulder.

147
00:10:26,447 --> 00:10:27,047
Why?

148
00:10:31,287 --> 00:10:36,847
Why did we ever have to meet?

149
00:10:48,067 --> 00:10:51,567
All right, volunteers, stay behind after the graduation ceremony.

150
00:10:55,007 --> 00:10:59,227
Uh, what's with all this work just for us to celebrate our teacher's wedding?

151
00:10:59,227 --> 00:11:01,387
It seems all a bit too much.

152
00:11:01,887 --> 00:11:05,227
Lest you forget, you're part of the action committee, so stop talking.

153
00:11:05,707 --> 00:11:08,367
Now make sure to return all the tools when you're done.

154
00:11:08,567 --> 00:11:09,707
They go in the back.

155
00:11:10,127 --> 00:11:10,607
What?

156
00:11:11,187 --> 00:11:11,667
Again?

157
00:11:12,087 --> 00:11:13,527
Hurry up and do it!

158
00:11:13,907 --> 00:11:14,507
Yes, ma'am?

159
00:11:15,547 --> 00:11:16,447
Hey, Hanabi.

160
00:11:16,707 --> 00:11:17,887
Let me help you out there.

161
00:11:18,467 --> 00:11:19,567
Uh, really?

162
00:11:20,467 --> 00:11:21,807
Uh, thanks for that.

163
00:11:22,647 --> 00:11:23,647
What's your...

164
00:11:23,647 --> 00:11:24,447
I'm Moriyama.

165
00:11:24,747 --> 00:11:25,707
We're in the same class.

166
00:11:26,027 --> 00:11:27,447
Well, starting this year, at least.

167
00:11:27,787 --> 00:11:29,047
Oh, yeah.

168
00:11:29,227 --> 00:11:30,467
Mm-hmm.

169
00:11:39,707 --> 00:11:41,767
Hanabi, you doing okay there?

170
00:11:42,247 --> 00:11:43,307
Let's just put these away.

171
00:11:43,827 --> 00:11:44,887
Yeah, sorry.

172
00:11:48,607 --> 00:11:51,007
Thanks again, with helping me and all.

173
00:11:51,367 --> 00:11:52,207
You saved me.

174
00:11:53,167 --> 00:11:54,047
Uh, sure.

175
00:11:54,467 --> 00:11:55,247
Listen, Hanabi.

176
00:11:55,727 --> 00:11:55,987
Huh?

177
00:11:56,507 --> 00:11:58,707
How have things been between you and Mugi?

178
00:11:59,547 --> 00:12:03,227
It's just that I haven't seen the two of you around each other lately.

179
00:12:05,467 --> 00:12:09,747
So, um, Hanabi, if you're interested, maybe you'd like to...

180
00:12:09,747 --> 00:12:10,667
Well, um...

181
00:12:10,667 --> 00:12:12,247
All right, that's enough from you.

182
00:12:13,347 --> 00:12:15,047
Hanabi belongs only to me.

183
00:12:15,627 --> 00:12:17,507
Now kindly back off of her, will ya?

184
00:12:17,627 --> 00:12:18,647
W-what?

185
00:12:18,647 --> 00:12:20,767
Let's go.

186
00:12:20,767 --> 00:12:21,207
Uh...

187
00:12:21,207 --> 00:12:23,207
Uh...

188
00:12:23,207 --> 00:12:24,207
Uh...

189
00:12:24,207 --> 00:12:25,207
Uh...

190
00:12:25,207 --> 00:12:26,327
Uh...

191
00:12:26,327 --> 00:12:26,647
Hmm.

192
00:12:28,647 --> 00:12:29,207
I...

193
00:12:29,207 --> 00:12:29,807
I...

194
00:12:29,807 --> 00:12:31,107
I'm sorry.

195
00:12:32,887 --> 00:12:33,887
But...

196
00:12:34,887 --> 00:12:38,887
It's appreciated very much.

197
00:12:38,887 --> 00:12:39,167
Oh.

198
00:12:39,167 --> 00:12:50,707
Hey, Sanai.

199
00:12:51,127 --> 00:12:51,987
Don't worry.

200
00:12:52,387 --> 00:12:53,947
I was just joking back there.

201
00:12:55,047 --> 00:12:57,007
Why did you come and rescue me?

202
00:12:57,727 --> 00:12:59,287
You still want your space?

203
00:12:59,847 --> 00:13:01,267
If I'm not mistaken?

204
00:13:02,607 --> 00:13:03,167
Yeah.

205
00:13:04,127 --> 00:13:05,087
That's correct.

206
00:13:05,087 --> 00:13:07,527
You're just the best.

207
00:13:07,527 --> 00:13:07,787
Huh?

208
00:13:08,027 --> 00:13:09,347
Why are you crying right now?

209
00:13:09,707 --> 00:13:11,207
You're so nice.

210
00:13:11,827 --> 00:13:13,947
You're always so nice, Sanai.

211
00:13:14,327 --> 00:13:15,487
Okay, okay.

212
00:13:15,747 --> 00:13:17,107
Just blow your nose already.

213
00:13:17,287 --> 00:13:18,047
I...

214
00:13:18,047 --> 00:13:18,927
I...

215
00:13:18,927 --> 00:13:21,767
I didn't think you would ever want to talk to me again.

216
00:13:21,767 --> 00:13:22,327
Hmm.

217
00:13:24,387 --> 00:13:25,987
I wouldn't do that to you.

218
00:13:27,047 --> 00:13:27,927
I'm sorry.

219
00:13:28,627 --> 00:13:30,427
I'm sorry it took so long.

220
00:13:30,427 --> 00:13:33,667
You cut your hair off.

221
00:13:35,567 --> 00:13:35,827
Hmm.

222
00:13:39,207 --> 00:13:41,027
You're the girl from the exam earlier.

223
00:13:41,487 --> 00:13:41,747
Huh?

224
00:13:43,387 --> 00:13:45,027
You didn't braid your hair today.

225
00:13:45,847 --> 00:13:46,927
Uh...

226
00:13:46,927 --> 00:13:48,087
Yeah, that was me.

227
00:13:48,807 --> 00:13:50,207
You mind if I touch your hair?

228
00:13:50,427 --> 00:13:50,647
Huh?

229
00:13:51,227 --> 00:13:51,487
Huh?

230
00:13:53,947 --> 00:13:54,427
Wow.

231
00:13:54,747 --> 00:13:55,967
Your hair is amazing.

232
00:13:55,967 --> 00:13:57,727
It looks so pretty down.

233
00:14:00,427 --> 00:14:03,067
At that very moment,

234
00:14:03,907 --> 00:14:06,287
I felt forgiven for some reason.

235
00:14:08,327 --> 00:14:11,787
It was like it was my first breath.

236
00:14:12,487 --> 00:14:14,527
The world looked down and took me in.

237
00:14:17,307 --> 00:14:17,707
And...

238
00:14:17,707 --> 00:14:20,207
Sanai...

239
00:14:20,207 --> 00:14:24,767
This hairstyle looks nice on you.

240
00:14:25,327 --> 00:14:26,327
But anything would.

241
00:14:26,327 --> 00:14:26,407
I don't know.

242
00:14:30,427 --> 00:14:43,227
I feel so refreshed now.

243
00:14:43,227 --> 00:15:03,227
It was nice of them to do this for us

244
00:15:03,227 --> 00:15:05,827
Wasn't it? I'm so embarrassed

245
00:15:05,827 --> 00:15:08,487
Here, we all signed a card for you

246
00:15:08,487 --> 00:15:10,507
Oh wow, thank you so much

247
00:15:10,507 --> 00:15:15,367
Hanabi, I heard you were invited to go to Mr. Kanai's wedding

248
00:15:15,367 --> 00:15:16,387
Did I get that right?

249
00:15:16,927 --> 00:15:17,927
Uh, yeah

250
00:15:17,927 --> 00:15:19,347
I'm so jealous

251
00:15:19,347 --> 00:15:22,807
I've never been invited to attend a real live wedding before

252
00:15:22,807 --> 00:15:24,847
This will be my first one, too

253
00:15:24,847 --> 00:15:31,347
Oh, that's the dream, isn't it?

254
00:15:31,347 --> 00:15:34,347
Spending the rest of your life with the person you truly love

255
00:15:34,347 --> 00:15:38,487
The dream?

256
00:15:38,487 --> 00:15:52,387
It's the bouquet toss

257
00:15:52,387 --> 00:16:06,447
It's the bouquet toss

258
00:16:06,447 --> 00:16:08,107
What? It's the toss

259
00:16:08,107 --> 00:16:10,227
Why are you not throwing the stupid thing?

260
00:16:10,347 --> 00:16:11,667
Just take it

261
00:16:11,667 --> 00:16:13,147
What are you doing to me?

262
00:16:13,767 --> 00:16:14,827
Take it

263
00:16:14,827 --> 00:16:16,347
Fine, are you happy now?

264
00:16:17,347 --> 00:16:17,907
Miss Akane?

265
00:16:21,507 --> 00:16:22,747
But next time

266
00:16:22,747 --> 00:16:25,207
Don't let him get stolen

267
00:16:25,207 --> 00:16:29,447
That's none of your concern anymore

268
00:16:29,447 --> 00:16:40,667
It turns out

269
00:16:40,667 --> 00:16:41,847
The promise we made

270
00:16:41,847 --> 00:16:44,267
And the days we spent together

271
00:16:44,267 --> 00:16:47,167
Had no meaning in the end

272
00:16:47,167 --> 00:16:59,347
In the beginning

273
00:16:59,347 --> 00:17:00,387
I was just lonely

274
00:17:00,387 --> 00:17:02,787
I wanted to be touched

275
00:17:02,787 --> 00:17:10,147
I ended up falling in love

276
00:17:10,147 --> 00:17:11,787
With your warmth

277
00:17:11,787 --> 00:17:15,447
Hanabi

278
